# Ryan's PERSONAL cognitive architecture — local-only, NEVER publish (PII: his
# daughter's name appears three times). Generated from his own interview, and it
# is keyed to the agent name "Sentinel", so it has no function in a public
# distribution: a user who names their agent anything else resolves default.md.
# default.md IS published — that is the template the first-run creator copies,
# and its absence is what made every first run fall back to a stale ryan.md.
prompts/cognitive-architectures/orchestrator/sentinel.md

# Operator-internal release runbook — local-only, NEVER publish.
# It names every build-time secret variable, states which conditions leave
# licence verification disabled, and documents the download kill-switch. No
# secret VALUES, but it is a map of the licence-enforcement seams.
# It was public from 2026-06-03 to 2026-08-05 because it was never listed here
# and a "publish the accumulated skill work" sweep picked it up. Remediated by
# deleting and recreating the repo (force-push alone does NOT remove orphaned
# objects — GitHub still serves them by SHA). Authoritative copy now lives at
# ~/.claude/skills/ls-release-litesuite/.
skills/ls-release-litesuite/
**/.liteeditor/
